IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `src-formulas`

-- Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 -- worked cases for the amounts computed from the formulas sidecar
-- (C2004A03668.formulas.md), from the seat of the injured employee.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand
-- from the formulas and the deposited text (C2026C00285), never copied from the encoding's output; the working is in the
-- comment above each case. No scenario life raised this Act; every case is HYPOTHETICAL. The indexed amounts used ($202,
-- $50, $25, $15,000) are the printed figures, standing in for the figures in force; the AWOTE and the rate per kilometre
-- are made-up figures, not published ones.
--
-- Tom (HYPOTHETICAL), an APS officer, 38 hours a week at $45 an hour ordinary time, with a $30 weekly allowance.

§ `cases`

§§ `s 8 -- normal weekly earnings`

-- The arguments: average weekly hours; hourly ordinary rate; weekly allowances; regular overtime; overtime hours; overtime rate.
-- Tom: (38 × 45) + 30 = 1,710 + 30 = 1,740.
#ASSERT `my normal weekly earnings under s 8` 38 45 30 FALSE 4 67.5 EQUALS 1740
-- Required to work 4 hours of overtime a week at $67.50: 1,740 + (4 × 67.50 = 270) = 2,010.
#ASSERT `my normal weekly earnings under s 8` 38 45 30 TRUE 4 67.5 EQUALS 2010
-- No allowances, part-time 20 hours at $40: 800.
#ASSERT `my normal weekly earnings under s 8` 20 40 0 FALSE 0 0 EQUALS 800

§§ `s 16(6)(c) -- travel to treatment`

-- The arguments: compensable; return distance; public transport or ambulance; reasonably required; rate per kilometre.
-- 120.6 km there and back by car at a (made-up) $0.80 a kilometre: whole kilometres, 120 × 0.80 = 96.
#ASSERT `How much for the journey to treatment` TRUE 120.6 FALSE FALSE 0.8 EQUALS 96
-- 40 km by car: not over 50 km (s 16(7)(a)), nothing.
#ASSERT `How much for the journey to treatment` TRUE 40 FALSE FALSE 0.8 EQUALS 0
-- 40 km by ambulance, which the injury reasonably required (s 16(7)(b)): 40 × 0.80 = 32.
#ASSERT `How much for the journey to treatment` TRUE 40 TRUE TRUE 0.8 EQUALS 32
-- Treatment Comcare is not paying for: nothing.
#ASSERT `How much for the journey to treatment` FALSE 120 FALSE FALSE 0.8 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 19 -- the weekly amount`

-- The arguments: incapacitated; normal weekly hours; hours prevented before this week; hours prevented this week; hours
-- employed this week; pension age reached; injured within 2 years of it; weeks compensated; in prison; NWE; able to earn
-- in suitable employment; earned this week; AWOTE; a prescribed person other than a child dependent; prescribed children
-- dependent; of them aged 16 or more; $202; $50; $25. AWOTE is a made-up $2,000 (cap $3,000) unless stated.
-- Week 11, totally off work: 380 + 38 = 418 hours, within 45 × 38 = 1,710, a maximum rate week; NWE − AE = 1,740 − 0.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 380 38 0 FALSE FALSE 10 FALSE 1740 0 0 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 1740
-- Back on 19 hours, earning $855 (and able to earn that): 1,740 − 855 = 885.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 380 19 19 FALSE FALSE 10 FALSE 1740 855 855 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 885
-- Offered suitable work at $2,000 a week (more than NWE): NWE − AE is negative, read as nil.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 380 38 0 FALSE FALSE 10 FALSE 1740 2000 0 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 0
-- Past the 1,710 hours, not employed: 75% × 1,740 = 1,305; minimum earnings min(202, 90% × 1,740 = 1,566) = 202, below it.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 1748 38 0 FALSE FALSE 46 FALSE 1740 0 0 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 1305
-- Past it, employed 19 of 38 hours (50%, so 85%), earning $855: 0.85 × 1,740 = 1,479; 1,479 − 855 = 624.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 1748 19 19 FALSE FALSE 46 FALSE 1740 855 855 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 624
-- A high earner, NWE $5,000, not employed: 75% × 5,000 = 3,750, over 150% × 2,000 = 3,000, reduced to 3,000 (s 19(5)).
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 1748 38 0 FALSE FALSE 46 FALSE 5000 0 0 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 3000
-- The s 19(5) cap applies only to the s 19(3) amount: in a maximum rate week the same earner gets 5,000.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 380 38 0 FALSE FALSE 10 FALSE 5000 0 0 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 5000
-- A low earner, NWE $600, not employed, able to earn $300: 0.75 × 600 − 300 = 150. With a dependent spouse and 2 children
-- under 16: minimum earnings min(202 + 50 + 2 × 25 = 302, 0.9 × 600 = 540) = 302, so raised to 302 (s 19(6)-(9)).
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 1748 38 0 FALSE FALSE 46 FALSE 600 300 0 2000 TRUE 2 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 302
-- The same with no dependants: min(202, 540) = 202.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 1748 38 0 FALSE FALSE 46 FALSE 600 300 0 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 202
-- The only dependant is a 17-year-old prescribed child (also a prescribed person): (10) takes it out of (9), so 202 + 50 = 252.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 1748 38 0 FALSE FALSE 46 FALSE 600 300 0 2000 FALSE 1 1 202 50 25 EQUALS 252
-- A spouse and 3 children, 2 of them 16 or more: (11) puts one of those under (8), the rest under (9): 202 + 50 + 2 × 25 = 302.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 1748 38 0 FALSE FALSE 46 FALSE 600 300 0 2000 TRUE 3 2 202 50 25 EQUALS 302
-- A spouse and 1 child of 17: neither (10) (the child is not the only prescribed person) nor (11) applies: 202 + 50 + 25 = 277.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 1748 38 0 FALSE FALSE 46 FALSE 600 300 0 2000 TRUE 1 1 202 50 25 EQUALS 277
-- Employed 9 of 38 hours (23.7%, so 80%), earning $100, able to earn $100: 0.8 × 600 − 100 = 380.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 1748 29 9 FALSE FALSE 46 FALSE 600 100 100 2000 TRUE 2 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 380
-- The same, but able to earn $400: 0.8 × 600 − 400 = 80, below the 302 minimum; but minimum earnings apply only under
-- s 19(3)(a), a week in which the employee is not employed, so 80 stands.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 1748 29 9 FALSE FALSE 46 FALSE 600 400 100 2000 TRUE 2 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 80
-- The split week (s 19(2B)-(2D)), totally off: 1,691 hours before, 38 this week, so 19 hours remain to 1,710: X = 19.
-- (19/38) × 1,740 = 870, plus (19/38) × 1,305 = 652.50: 1,522.50.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 1691 38 0 FALSE FALSE 44 FALSE 1740 0 0 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 1522.5
-- A split week, partly off: 40 normal hours (45 × 40 = 1,800), 1,790 before, 20 prevented this week, working 20 hours for
-- $1,000. X = 40 × (10 / 20) = 20. Maximum rate 2,000 − 1,000 = 1,000; reduced (20/40 = 50%, so 85%) 1,700 − 1,000 = 700.
-- (20/40) × 1,000 + (20/40) × 700 = 500 + 350 = 850.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 40 1790 20 20 FALSE FALSE 45 FALSE 2000 1000 1000 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 850
-- No amount where src-employee.l4 gives none: pension age reached (s 23(1)), or not incapacitated.
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` TRUE 38 3000 38 0 TRUE FALSE 80 FALSE 1740 0 0 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much weekly compensation this week` FALSE 38 380 0 38 FALSE FALSE 10 FALSE 1740 0 1740 2000 FALSE 0 0 202 50 25 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 27 -- non-economic loss`

-- The arguments: kind of impairment; degree of permanent impairment; binaural hearing loss; degree of non-economic loss; $15,000 in force.
-- 20% impairment, 30% non-economic loss: (15,000 × 20%) + (15,000 × 30%) = 3,000 + 4,500 = 7,500.
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `another impairment` 20 0 30 15000 EQUALS 7500
-- 8% impairment: below the s 24(7) threshold, no s 24 compensation, so none under s 27.
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `another impairment` 8 0 30 15000 EQUALS 0
-- A hearing loss of 6% (binaural 6%, at least 5%), non-economic loss 10%: 900 + 1,500 = 2,400.
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `a hearing loss` 6 6 10 15000 EQUALS 2400
-- The loss of a finger, 3%, no threshold (s 24(8)); non-economic loss 5%: 450 + 750 = 1,200.
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `the loss, or loss of use, of a finger or toe, or the loss of the sense of taste or smell` 3 0 5 15000 EQUALS 1200

§§ `ss 13, 13AA -- indexation`

-- The arguments: later index number; earlier index number.
-- 140.0 / 135.0 = 1.03703...: 3 places 1.037, 4th place 0, not over 4: 1.037.
#ASSERT `the indexation factor to 3 places` 140 135 EQUALS 1.037
-- 103.75 / 100 = 1.0375: 4th place 5, over 4: 1.037 + 0.001 = 1.038.
#ASSERT `the indexation factor to 3 places` 103.75 100 EQUALS 1.038
-- 103.74 / 100 = 1.0374: 4th place 4, not over 4: 1.037.
#ASSERT `the indexation factor to 3 places` 103.74 100 EQUALS 1.037
-- The arguments: index; amount before; December quarter index before the year; the one a year earlier.
-- $80,000 (s 24(9)) on CPI 140.0 over 135.0: 80,000 × 1.037 = 82,960.
#ASSERT `the amount after a year's indexation` `the Consumer Price Index (s 13: the amounts in ss 18(4)(a), 19(7) to (9), 24(9), 27(2), 29, 30(1), 137(1))` 80000 140 135 EQUALS 82960
-- $15,000 (s 27(2)) on a factor of 1.038: 15,570.
#ASSERT `the amount after a year's indexation` `the Consumer Price Index (s 13: the amounts in ss 18(4)(a), 19(7) to (9), 24(9), 27(2), 29, 30(1), 137(1))` 15000 103.75 100 EQUALS 15570
-- $400,000 (s 17(3)) on a WPI that fell, 99 over 100: the factor is not greater than one, no substitution.
#ASSERT `the amount after a year's indexation` `the Wage Price Index (s 13AA: the amounts in s 17(3) to (5))` 400000 99 100 EQUALS 400000
-- A flat index, 100 over 100: factor 1, not greater than one, no substitution.
#ASSERT `the amount after a year's indexation` `the Wage Price Index (s 13AA: the amounts in s 17(3) to (5))` 400000 100 100 EQUALS 400000
-- $400,000 on WPI 104.2 over 100 = 1.042: 416,800.
#ASSERT `the amount after a year's indexation` `the Wage Price Index (s 13AA: the amounts in s 17(3) to (5))` 400000 104.2 100 EQUALS 416800
-- Two years running, chained (s 13AA(2)(a), the last substituted amount): 416,800 on 108.4 over 104.2 = 1.04030...: 1.040; 416,800 × 1.04 = 433,472.
#ASSERT `the amount after a year's indexation` `the Wage Price Index (s 13AA: the amounts in s 17(3) to (5))` 416800 108.4 104.2 EQUALS 433472
